id: pm-github-t4i2
title: Close pm items delivered by merged pull requests with verifiable GitHub evidence
description: "Add a safe, idempotent pm github closeout command so agents can close delivered tracker items using facts verified against merged pull requests and head checks."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[1]: changelog-unreleased
created_at: "2026-10-14T21:42:54.457Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T03:52:15.943Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-15T03:52:15.924Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-15T03:48:51.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Resolve the existing repository and select repeatable --pr numbers or merged PRs at or after --since ISO time; dry-run by default, --apply writes, compact TOON and stable --json plan rows item/pr/action/reason.; Extract only same-repository .agents/pm/<folder>/<id>.toon links; report foreign-repository links and unknown ids as explicit skips; never import PR body or comment text.; Skip closed/canceled items and repeatable --skip ids; require merged PR and successful required head checks; missing/failed check evidence fails closed; unreadable protection falls back to all head runs completed with success/neutral/skipped and reports the applied rule.; Use the SDK close path with only PR number/URL, merge commit SHA, head SHA, merge time and passed head check names in the close reason; repeated selection performs zero additional tracker writes.; Test with existing GitHub HTTP fixtures and real temporary trackers: repository matching, unknown/terminal/skipped ids, failed required checks, missing evidence, fallback, dry-run byte equality, exact apply reason, repeated no-op and synthetic email/token privacy; demonstrate behavioral revert failures for check gating and idempotency.; Document agent examples and pm-changelog entry; optionally add a separate bot-branch closeout workflow only after complete tests, otherwise create a follow-up item; keep gated sync workflow and inputs unchanged.; Pass npm and Bun release:check with isolated Git identity and unchanged thresholds; regenerate and check changelog; commit tracker/history with code, push branch and open the requested public-safe PR without closing this item."
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T21:45:11.970Z",codex-agent,"Specification recorded before implementation. Plan: reuse repository/token resolution and REST transport; read a certified complete SDK corpus; build the entire dry-run plan before writes; use SDK close only for merged PRs with verified head evidence. Required contexts include check runs and legacy statuses with app constraints. Protection 403/404 uses an explicit conservative fallback. No trailer syntax. Close reasons contain only structured GitHub facts. Keep the reusable sync workflow unchanged and track optional automation separately."
  "2026-10-14T21:49:46.159Z",codex-agent,Implemented dry-run planning and SDK close with exact JSON GitHub facts. Initial focused acceptance passed 49/49 plus packed CLI and real registration checks 2/2. Added active ruleset context checks so classic protection cannot omit a ruleset requirement; verifying pagination and malformed evidence next. Optional reusable bot-branch automation is tracked in pm-github-0x3y.
  "2026-10-14T21:56:49.634Z",codex-agent,"Focused HTTP/real-tracker acceptance: 58/58 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled/TODO; closeout.ts exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Behavioral guard-revert proofs: removing only the required-success rejection in checkCloseoutHead made node --test --test-name-pattern=\"required check gate rejects failed evidence\" test/closeout.test.ts fail 1/1 (a failed required check closed an item). Restored it. Removing only the terminal-item branch in runCloseout made node --test --test-name-pattern=\"apply persists only exact GitHub reason facts; repeated selection writes zero bytes\" test/closeout.test.ts fail 1/1 (repeat attempted SDK close and errored). Restored it. Both regressions then passed 2/2 with the original source restored. These tests import source directly. Native Bun registration acceptance passed 1/1 with the repository-standard explicit timeout."
  "2026-10-14T21:58:06.666Z",codex-agent,"The linked acceptance command completed successfully through pm test --run --progress: 1/1 linked commands passed with no failures, skips or infrastructure errors. Native Bun registration acceptance also passed. The isolated npm release gate is now running; the pinned SDK, package thresholds, and reusable sync workflow remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-14T22:30:45.294Z",codex-agent,"The isolated npm release gate completed its full test phase: 648/648 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled/TODO. Coverage aggregation and final release steps are pending; the executable source has not changed. Bun release:check will run next with a separate isolated Git identity."
  "2026-10-14T22:36:16.724Z",codex-agent,"Isolated npm release:check PASSED: 648/648 tests, zero failed/skipped/canceled/TODO, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 13 authored modules, zero production vulnerabilities, and passing build/typecheck/docstring/lint/duplication/privacy/pack/changelog/attestation checks. The isolated Bun release gate is running next; executable source and thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-14T22:49:57.242Z",codex-agent,"Review found that repository validation rejected valid leading-dot repository names such as .github. Added an HTTP/real-tracker regression, confirmed it fails against the strict validation, then corrected the shape guard while explicitly rejecting dot and dot-dot path segments. The earlier 648-test npm gate validated the prior source and is superseded for delivery; the in-progress Bun gate was stopped for this correction. Both full gates will be rerun on the corrected source."
  "2026-10-14T23:27:07.100Z",codex-agent,"SDK contract review found two additional edge cases. Real custom types may use dotted, space-containing or nested tracker folders; the earlier extraction matcher missed them. Supplemental rules failures could also relax readable required-check protection to the neutral/skipped fallback. Both new HTTP/real-tracker regressions failed against the earlier functions, then passed after corrections (4/4 targeted checks, including real custom-type SDK closes). Canonical path components are now decoded and traversal/malformed encodings rejected. Fallback is restricted to unreadable classic protection; supplemental failures with readable classic protection fail closed. The intermediate 649-test npm gate passed but is superseded for delivery. Fresh full gates will validate these corrections."
  "2026-10-14T23:49:22.138Z",codex-agent,"The final metadata policy reads classic protection and active rulesets independently. Every readable required context remains mandatory even in fallback; missing permission/not-found metadata adds the conservative all-head-runs rule without discarding known requirements. Tests proved the earlier implementation could ignore readable rulesets when classic protection was unavailable, and could hide a second-source authorization failure. Those regressions now pass along with the inverse partial-permission cases (5/5 targeted). This refines the prior note: supplemental permission gaps may use fallback only while retaining all known required-check constraints. Malformed metadata and non-permission API errors still fail closed. The complete closeout suite now has 64 cases."
  "2026-10-14T23:56:52.792Z",codex-agent,"Final candidate preflight: 64/64 focused cases passed with zero failed/skipped/canceled/TODO and exact 100/100/100/100 coverage for closeout.ts. Refreshed behavioral guard removals each failed their targeted regression 1/1; restoring the original source passed both 2/2. Native Bun acceptance passed 2/2, including real SDK closes in dotted, encoded-space and nested folders. Production source is now fixed for the linked test run and sequential isolated npm/Bun release gates. SDK pins, thresholds and reusable sync workflow remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-15T00:14:01.917Z",codex-agent,"The full frozen-source gate exposed an existing watchdog startup race: the synthetic child did not print ready before its unchanged 500 ms deadline. The isolated watchdog suite passed 2/2. The failed attempt was stopped and is not passing evidence. Follow-up pm-github-sah1 tracks deterministic startup probing; no helper code, deadline, coverage threshold or production source was changed. Both complete release gates will rerun with bounded file-worker concurrency through a controlled process affinity profile."
  "2026-10-15T00:45:37.106Z",codex-agent,"Frozen-source npm release:check PASSED under the bounded worker profile: 654/654 tests, zero failed/skipped/canceled/TODO, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 13 authored modules, zero production vulnerabilities, and all remaining release checks passed. The existing watchdog probe passed at its original 500 ms deadline. Source and all thresholds/deadlines are unchanged; the isolated Bun gate is running in sequence. Earlier interrupted or superseded runs are not delivery evidence."
  "2026-10-15T01:06:06.994Z",codex-agent,"DELIVERY CANDIDATE VERIFIED: isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check both PASSED on the frozen source, each 654/654 tests with zero failed/skipped/canceled/TODO, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across 13 authored modules, zero production vulnerabilities, and all build/type/docstring/lint/duplication/privacy/pack/changelog/attestation checks green. Bounded worker concurrency preserved every test and deadline; the watchdog passed in both full runs. Focused acceptance is 64/64, linked pm tests 1/1 commands, native Bun 2/2, and both refreshed guard-removal proofs failed before restoration and passed 2/2 after restoration. Optional workflow remains pm-github-0x3y; deterministic watchdog startup remains pm-github-sah1. The reusable sync workflow, inputs, SDK pins and thresholds are unchanged. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification without closing this feature."
  "2026-10-15T01:16:45.243Z",claude-hub,"Orchestrator verification with real data (2026-10-15), on a scratch clone of the pm-jev tracker, installed from the packed tarball. The first implementation closed EVERY linked non-terminal item. A dry run over pm-jev PRs 1, 7 and 17 planned to close the pm-jev epic and four open follow-ups (live acceptance pending an API key, the deferred Rust client, and two audit follow-ups) that PR 1 only linked for context. Fixed: a link alone never closes an item. An item closes only when it is in_progress (claimed work) or its link follows a GitHub-style closing keyword (Closes, Fixes, Resolves, Delivers) on the same line, and it is neither an Epic nor the parent of a non-terminal child. Every refusal gets a skip row naming the rule. The same dry run now closes only pm-jev-2mg8 (delivered by PR 17). Apply in the scratch clone wrote a close reason containing only GitHub facts (PR, URL, merge commit, head, merge time, passing checks), and a second apply closed 0. New test 'a mention is not delivery: open follow-ups, epics and parents with active children are never closed' fails when the rules are removed (behavioural revert, 0 of 1 pass); test/closeout.test.ts passes 65 of 65."
  "2026-10-15T02:17:59.088Z",claude-hub,"Review round 2 (PR 124, CodeRabbit on bfaf0f2), fixed by the orchestrator. (1) Major: the closing keyword matched anywhere earlier on the line, so prose such as 'Not fixed here; see <link>' declared delivery. declaresDelivery now scans backwards from the link with plain string operations and accepts the keyword only when nothing but earlier links (markdown or bare), commas and 'and' sit between them; colons and emphasis around the keyword are allowed. The three reported lines and further edge cases are regression-tested. (2) since now stops paging once a row was last updated before the cutoff, because rows arrive newest-updated first and a merge never postdates the PR update. (3) The command handler maps closeout failures to CommandError (selector and repository errors give USAGE exit 2, everything else GENERIC_FAILURE exit 1), so the host no longer re-runs the handler and repeats GitHub reads or remaining closes. Behavioural revert proofs: each of the three changes, removed alone, fails its new test."
